STATUS 2026-08-11: scope breakdown documented. Not started; out of session
scope. Sub-tickets 29a-29e PROPOSED, not auto-created — maintainer splits
when ready (precedent: karr #28 same flow).

Scope: Self-hosted inference engines (vLLM, SGLang, LlamaCpp, Ollama)
expose Prometheus /metrics endpoints. Langfuse observability already
exists via Role::Langfuse but is connection-side (trace/span). This
ticket adds a server-side scraper that surfaces inference-runtime metrics
into Langfuse or compatible OTLP.

Proposed sub-tickets:
  29a — research: each engine's /metrics endpoint contract
        vLLM: /metrics (Prometheus text, http.* + vllm:* keys)
        SGLang: /metrics (Prometheus text, sglang:* keys)
        LlamaCpp: /metrics (Prometheus text, llama_* keys)
        Ollama: per /api/ps (JSON, not Prometheus — needs adapter)
  29b — class: Langertha::Runtime::Metrics — Prometheus text format
        parser with engine-key allowlist
  29c — role: Langertha::Role::Runtime::MetricsPoll on
        Engine::VLLM, Engine::SGLang, Engine::LlamaCpp, Engine::Ollama
        (using attributes already required for those engines: url, optional api_key)
  29d — bridge: convert scraped Prometheus → Langfuse OTLP metrics
        (re-use Role::Langfuse endpoint); alternative is direct
        Prometheus remote_write adapter (separate ticket)
  29e — tests: offline scrape-fixture → parse → bridge → asserting
        metric-name passthrough; live gated on running engine (no API
        key needed, requires local vLLM/SGLang server)

Out of scope (separate tickets):
  - Remote-write adapter (push scraped metrics to a Prometheus server)
  - Langfuse metrics-generation API integration
  - OpenAI/Anthropic usage accounting (covered by Langertha::Usage/Response.usage)
